### Sum of Beauty of All Substrings

**Problem:** Given a string, calculate the sum of beauty values of all its substrings. The beauty of a substring is defined as the difference between the frequency of the most frequent character and the frequency of the least frequent character (excluding characters that do not appear).

**Approach:**
- Initialize a variable `sum` to store the total beauty of all substrings.
- Traverse the string using an outer loop to select the starting index of each substring.
- Create a frequency array of size 26 to track the occurrences of each character.
- Use an inner loop to extend the substring from the starting index.
- Update the frequency of the current character.
- Find the maximum and minimum frequencies among the characters present in the current substring.
- Calculate the beauty by subtracting the minimum frequency from the maximum frequency.
- Add the beauty value to the total sum.
- Return the final sum.

**Time Complexity:** O(n² × 26) – We generate all substrings and calculate the maximum and minimum character frequencies.

**Space Complexity:** O(26) = O(1) – A fixed-size frequency array is used.

**Concepts Used:**
- String Traversal
- Nested Loops
- Frequency Counting
- Hashing
- Character Frequency Array
- Substring Manipulation

###Solution


class Solution {
    public int beautySum(String s) {
        int n = s.length();
        int sum = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            int[] freq = new int[26];
            int max = 0;
            for (int j = i; j < n; j++) {
                int index=s.charAt(j)-'a';
                freq[index]++;
                max=Math.max(max,freq[index]);
                
                int min = Integer.MAX_VALUE;
                for (int k = 0; k < 26; k++) {
                    if (freq[k] > 0) {
                        min = Math.min(min, freq[k]);
                    }
                }
                sum += (max - min);
            }
        }

        return sum;
    }
}
